## Lore

Biomancers live in complete symbiosis with the ecosystem around them, meeting
their needs without tools, machines or harm to any living thing. Their magic
depends on an intimate bond with nature and a profound regard for life, which
is why it is almost unknown across the Megaverse: its strongholds are the
jungle elves'' Green World and, through the elves, Rifts Earth - above all South
America, with a few wanderers in North America, Africa and Europe.

Biomancy is the philosophical opposite of necromancy, and the two schools are
mortal enemies. Biomancers despise Splugorth bio-wizardry as a mockery of life
and will never touch rune weapons. Technology is a "dead thing" to them, viewed
with distrust at best.

## The Three Philosophies

The Acceptors tolerate most of civilization''s harm to nature as part of
evolution and object only to its worst excesses; they live near cities, ride in
vehicles and use some technology, but shun cybernetics, bio-wizardry and rune
weapons, and are vegetarians. The Patient Ones refuse to accept such crimes,
live in all-natural communities, repair what others damage and defend claimed
lands, using technology only as a last resort; most on Maga Island are of this
school. The Defenders are militant: they reject technology outright, some wage
war on polluters and loggers, and they punish those who destroy life for
pleasure or profit.

## Alignment

Any, but most are principled, scrupulous, unprincipled or aberrant; the few
anarchist, miscreant or diabolic Biomancers are regarded as renegades.
Acceptors lean scrupulous or unprincipled, Patient Ones principled or aberrant,
and Defenders run the whole range.

## GM Notes

In Wormwood, a GM decides whether biomancy works on the living planet; plant
and animal powers are unlikely to. The Biomancer can commune with the planet as
a Wormspeaker does, plus life fuel, locate food and resources and repel
symbiotes, all at half range and duration.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'biomancer');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'biomancer';

